    {
      "id": "PGM-01",
      "chapter": "global",
      "anchor": "global-primitive-row-weights",
      "title": "The count at an exact determinant is an invariant genus observable",
      "statement": "Counting E-hyperplanes U with discriminant order d² on L∩U gives an isometry invariant. The weighted row sum times the positive genus mass equals the total row weight times the sum of these counts divided by automorphism orders.",
      "hypotheses": "A valid frame, finite row representatives, the totally definite complement, and the designated completely split prime Tᵤ≥3. The empty family is treated separately.",
      "correspondence": "Two applications of the row-weight identity, with the observable and with one, remove the common multiplicity.",
