    {
      "id": "PGM-02",
      "chapter": "global",
      "anchor": "global-primitive-gluing",
      "title": "Marking the hyperplane first reduces the mass bound to a rank-j and a rank-one mass",
      "statement": "For j=k−1 the unnormalized marked mass is at most MⱼM₁ d^(j+2+b) · t²d² · (dt)^(2+b), where b=log₂ f and t=Tᵤ^f.",
      "hypotheses": "The row genus has dual quotient cyclic as an 𝒪_E-module with t² additive elements annihilated by Tᵤ, norm((Tᵤ))=t². The source uses the maximal mass estimate, positive definite Hermitian spaces, the orthonormal-lattice supplier and the line-gluing bound.",
      "correspondence": "Count pairs of a lattice and a marked subspace, split into intersections in the hyperplane and orthogonal line, and bound the fibres of the gluing map. The finite Gaussian example checks orbit-stabilizer weights for a single lattice.",
